# Session logs (audit trail)

For any non-trivial work (anything that changes code or config and would become
a PR), maintain a session log in `docs/sessionLogs/`. This is our committed
audit trail of *why* changes were made.

## When to create one

- Start a log as soon as the work is clearly non-trivial (multi-step, a real
  decision, or a future PR). Skip it for pure questions, reads, or trivial
  one-line fixes.
- One log per unit of work / PR. If continuing earlier work, update the
  existing log rather than starting a new one.

## How

1. Copy `docs/sessionLogs/TEMPLATE.md` to
   `docs/sessionLogs/YYYY-MM-DD-<kebab-slug>.md`.
2. Fill it in **as you work**, while reasoning is fresh — not only at the end.
   Capture decisions and tradeoffs at the moment they happen.
3. Keep it curated and skimmable: focus on the WHY (goal, approach,
   alternatives, decisions, tradeoffs, follow-ups), not a play-by-play of the
   code. Do not paste raw transcripts.
4. Never include secrets, tokens, or credentials.
5. Commit the log in the same change set as the code it documents.

If you made meaningful decisions during a session and no log was created or
updated, treat that as incomplete work and write the log before finishing.
